the two main types of database schema.

13
00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:44.561
You then moved on to explore
relational database design.

14
00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:49.040
In this lesson, you learned how
to design a relational database.

15
00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:53.766
Having completed this lesson, you should
now be able to describe the relational

16
00:00:53.766 --> 00:00:58.982
model, list different types of relations,
evaluate an entity relationship diagram,

17
00:00:58.982 --> 00:01:02.961
or ERD, and explain the purpose of
primary key in a database table.

18
00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:06.869
And you should now also be
able to demonstrate how

19
00:01:06.869 --> 00:01:10.462
to select a single primary key,
and a composite primary key.

20
00:01:10.462 --> 00:01:14.958
Describe the purpose of a foreign key,
connect tables using a foreign key, and

21
00:01:14.958 --> 00:01:19.340
